WHY THESE PARAMETERS WERE SELECTED:

n_estimators:

Controls the number of trees. Values such as 50, 100, and 200 allow us to test whether adding more trees improves prediction stability.

max_depth:

Controls how deep each tree can grow. Limiting the depth can reduce overfitting.

min_samples_split:

Controls the minimum number of samples required to split a node. Larger values can create simpler trees.

min_samples_leaf:

Controls the minimum number of samples required in a leaf node. Increasing this value can prevent the tree from learning very small or noisy patterns.


