FINAL CONCLUSION:

GridSearchCV systematically tests all specified hyperparameter combinations, while RandomizedSearchCV tests a limited random selection and can therefore be faster.

SMOTE can help models learn from imbalanced datasets by creating synthetic minority-class examples. Another approach is class_weight="balanced", which gives more importance to minority-class observations without generating new samples.

For highly imbalanced classification problems, metrics such as F1-score, precision, and recall should be considered alongside accuracy because high accuracy does not necessarily mean that the minority class is being detected correctly.
